1
00:00:15,203 --> 00:00:17,371
HA JUNG-WOO

2
00:00:17,372 --> 00:00:19,374
IM SOO-JUNG

3
00:00:22,753 --> 00:00:25,005
KIM JUN-HAN

4
00:00:25,422 --> 00:00:27,257
KRYSTAL JUNG

5
00:00:33,513 --> 00:00:35,641
SHIM EUN-KYUNG

6
00:00:54,576 --> 00:00:58,955
MAD CONCRETE DREAMS

7
00:00:59,915 --> 00:01:01,791
TEN YEARS AGO

8
00:01:01,792 --> 00:01:04,252
Groom Min Hwal-sung, Bride Jeon Yi-gyeong
Congratulations on your wedding

9
00:01:08,298 --> 00:01:09,590
Da-rae is here.

10
00:01:09,591 --> 00:01:11,051
Do we really have to go to
the wedding afterparty too?

11
00:01:11,677 --> 00:01:13,744
It's Hwal-sung's wedding.
How can I not go?

12
00:01:13,745 --> 00:01:16,748
I was the emcee,
and I even got this golf bag.

13
00:01:18,433 --> 00:01:19,184
Da-rae,

14
00:01:19,309 --> 00:01:20,810
Have some odeng.

15
00:01:20,811 --> 00:01:22,020
Odeng.

16
00:01:23,188 --> 00:01:23,855
Yes.

17
00:01:24,648 --> 00:01:26,274
Gi Su-jong, it's been a long time.

18
00:01:26,566 --> 00:01:28,985
- Jeong Man-sik, you were here too?
- Of course, I had to come.

19
00:01:29,861 --> 00:01:31,987
- Long time no see, Seon.
- Yes.

20
00:01:31,988 --> 00:01:32,906
This guy here.

21
00:01:33,281 --> 00:01:35,617
- Hey, you look the same.
- I do.

22
00:01:36,451 --> 00:01:38,494
Oh my.

23
00:01:38,495 --> 00:01:40,622
What was your name again?

24
00:01:42,207 --> 00:01:44,126
Da-rae. Her name is Gi Da-rae.

25
00:01:45,544 --> 00:01:46,420
Da-rae,

26
00:01:46,962 --> 00:01:47,789
say hello.

27
00:01:49,423 --> 00:01:54,177
Hello, my name is Gi Da-rae.

28
00:01:55,804 --> 00:01:57,555
What a cute kid!

29
00:01:57,556 --> 00:01:59,640
Hey, you can talk quietly.

30
00:01:59,641 --> 00:02:00,892
She can read your lips.

31
00:02:01,768 --> 00:02:02,686
Really?

32
00:02:03,186 --> 00:02:05,230
Then can I have a drink... No, wait.

33
00:02:06,523 --> 00:02:07,691
Can I get a soda?

34
00:02:16,908 --> 00:02:18,368
Okay.

35
00:02:19,202 --> 00:02:20,620
You want soda too?

36
00:02:21,872 --> 00:02:22,872
Oh!

37
00:02:22,873 --> 00:02:24,207
She can't have sweets.

38
00:02:24,374 --> 00:02:25,374
Oh...

39
00:02:25,375 --> 00:02:26,376
No, she can't.

40
00:02:26,668 --> 00:02:27,586
Da-rae.

41
00:02:29,171 --> 00:02:30,172
Oh, right.

42
00:02:35,969 --> 00:02:37,553
Hey, the groom is here!

43
00:02:37,554 --> 00:02:38,722
Oh!

44
00:02:44,144 --> 00:02:45,020
Yes!

45
00:02:45,562 --> 00:02:46,688
Congratulations on the wedding!

46
00:02:51,067 --> 00:02:52,235
Okay.

47
00:02:53,028 --> 00:02:55,654
Since I'm the last to get married,

48
00:02:55,655 --> 00:02:56,406
I'll keep it short.

49
00:02:58,617 --> 00:03:00,452
Didn't you tell me not to marry young?

50
00:03:01,328 --> 00:03:02,871
- What are you talking about?
- Come on!

51
00:03:03,330 --> 00:03:06,208
The last one laughing
is the true winner.

52
00:03:09,461 --> 00:03:11,337
Min Hwal-sung, come on!

53
00:03:11,338 --> 00:03:12,923
Yes, thanks for the jeers.

54
00:03:13,757 --> 00:03:16,133
Anyway, I really appreciate everyone
for coming together like this.

55
00:03:16,134 --> 00:03:17,052
Um,

56
00:03:17,677 --> 00:03:19,720
but there's one thing

57
00:03:19,721 --> 00:03:20,764
I really wanted to say.

58
00:03:22,682 --> 00:03:25,477
My best friend, Su-jong.

59
00:03:27,229 --> 00:03:28,312
Whoa!

60
00:03:28,313 --> 00:03:29,105
Please stand up.

61
00:03:33,109 --> 00:03:33,944
Whoa!

62
00:03:38,615 --> 00:03:40,242
If it weren't for you, I wouldn't be here.

63
00:03:41,827 --> 00:03:43,662
Thanks so much
for presiding at the wedding today.

64
00:03:46,832 --> 00:03:48,166
- What's wrong?
- Oh, come on.

65
00:03:54,256 --> 00:03:55,715
Let's be friends forever.

66
00:03:58,802 --> 00:04:00,470
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

67
00:04:01,847 --> 00:04:03,348
Yi-gyeong,
congratulations on your wedding.

68
00:04:04,724 --> 00:04:09,395
Now, for Su-jong
and his wife and for Da-rae,

69
00:04:09,396 --> 00:04:11,106
how about a song?

70
00:04:11,857 --> 00:04:13,900
Wow!

71
00:04:17,737 --> 00:04:18,405
Yes!

72
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:30,125
Yeah!

73
00:04:35,839 --> 00:04:36,798
Applause.

74
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:49,436
Yeah!

75
00:04:52,898 --> 00:04:56,108
♪ No, this isn't right
Why can't I stop thinking about her? ♪

76
00:04:56,109 --> 00:04:59,070
♪ Should I like my friend's girl? ♪

77
00:04:59,404 --> 00:05:06,785
♪ I shouldn't feel this way,
yet all I do is think about her ♪

78
00:05:06,786 --> 00:05:13,334
♪ Why does her call make me so excited? ♪

79
00:05:13,335 --> 00:05:19,882
♪ I could just turn her down,
but why can't I? ♪

80
00:05:19,883 --> 00:05:23,761
♪ I'm really losing it ♪

81
00:05:23,762 --> 00:05:27,264
♪ I don't even know myself anymore ♪

82
00:05:27,265 --> 00:05:33,938
♪ Ignoring my long-time friendship
because of a girl ♪

83
00:05:33,939 --> 00:05:41,153
♪ It's so painful,
I just need to give up ♪

84
00:05:41,154 --> 00:05:47,159
♪ Why bother with something that
shouldn't even matter? ♪

85
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:47,910
All together!

86
00:05:47,911 --> 00:05:55,042
♪ I'm sorry, my friend
I deceived you for a moment ♪

87
00:05:55,043 --> 00:06:01,590
♪ My friendship with you
still feels a bit lacking ♪

88
00:06:01,591 --> 00:06:09,014
♪ Understand me, my friend
Our friendship shook for a bit ♪

89
00:06:09,015 --> 00:06:15,521
♪ Someone might be jealous
and testing our friendship ♪

90
00:06:15,522 --> 00:06:20,402
♪ Just think of it that way ♪

91
00:06:30,161 --> 00:06:37,460
MAD CONCRETE DREAMS

92
00:06:38,503 --> 00:06:40,964
EPISODE 7

93
00:06:43,466 --> 00:06:44,925
- Wow.
- What do you think?

94
00:06:44,926 --> 00:06:45,760
How do you like it?

95
00:06:46,261 --> 00:06:48,054
Oh, what can I say?

96
00:06:50,015 --> 00:06:51,390
But,

97
00:06:51,391 --> 00:06:52,684
why are we here?

98
00:06:53,309 --> 00:06:54,269
Seon,

99
00:06:55,061 --> 00:06:56,229
just give me three years.

100
00:06:56,855 --> 00:06:58,313
I'll buy this place

101
00:06:58,314 --> 00:06:59,357
and put it in your name.

102
00:07:15,331 --> 00:07:17,041
So, have you seen
the entire house?

103
00:07:17,042 --> 00:07:17,958
Yes.

104
00:07:17,959 --> 00:07:20,320
- It's so nice here, right?
- It's nice.

105
00:07:20,503 --> 00:07:22,922
Boss, just go ahead.

106
00:07:24,132 --> 00:07:26,092
- I should.
- Come this way.

107
00:07:26,426 --> 00:07:29,219
For this view, the space is limited here.

108
00:07:29,220 --> 00:07:30,179
Wow.

109
00:07:30,180 --> 00:07:32,264
This is really nice

110
00:07:32,265 --> 00:07:34,141
Right?
You can see all the way across.

111
00:07:34,142 --> 00:07:37,187
And the transportation is great.

112
00:07:46,571 --> 00:07:47,739
What's going on?

113
00:07:48,406 --> 00:07:49,532
Is Da-rae not home?

114
00:07:49,908 --> 00:07:53,036
Oh, she's watching a movie
with friends today.

115
00:07:53,870 --> 00:07:55,371
- Honey, you go wash up first.
- Okay.

116
00:07:56,539 --> 00:07:57,998
Seon,

117
00:07:57,999 --> 00:07:59,084
let's take a shower together.

118
00:08:02,087 --> 00:08:03,004
What?

119
00:08:03,755 --> 00:08:04,798
I mean,

120
00:08:06,341 --> 00:08:07,425
it's been a while.

121
00:08:07,967 --> 00:08:08,802
Should we...

122
00:08:12,430 --> 00:08:13,389
do it?

123
00:08:26,111 --> 00:08:27,237
Da-rae, you're back?

124
00:08:27,403 --> 00:08:29,697
Yes, Da-rae.

125
00:08:30,990 --> 00:08:32,200
Go and...

126
00:08:32,909 --> 00:08:33,785
shower.

127
00:08:35,411 --> 00:08:36,246
Shower.

128
00:08:41,042 --> 00:08:41,918
Okay.

129
00:08:58,143 --> 00:08:59,643
ASSISTANT NAM SANG-HOGood job.

130
00:08:59,644 --> 00:09:01,396
I have a good eye for people.

131
00:09:03,940 --> 00:09:05,525
I'll do better moving forward.

132
00:09:22,250 --> 00:09:22,876
Hey.

133
00:09:29,007 --> 00:09:29,966
Are you happy?

134
00:09:35,430 --> 00:09:36,389
Hwal-sung.

135
00:09:37,307 --> 00:09:38,224
What happened?

136
00:09:42,437 --> 00:09:43,271
My friend,

137
00:09:43,730 --> 00:09:45,814
what's with you riding both outside
and inside?

138
00:09:45,815 --> 00:09:48,483
Are you some kind of cyclist?

139
00:09:48,484 --> 00:09:49,943
Wait...

140
00:09:49,944 --> 00:09:51,613
What's going on? How did you get out?

141
00:09:51,946 --> 00:09:53,072
You think I would know?

142
00:09:54,908 --> 00:09:56,826
I just suddenly woke up.

143
00:09:57,452 --> 00:09:59,703
By the way,

144
00:09:59,704 --> 00:10:01,414
did you know who I thought of first?

145
00:10:05,335 --> 00:10:06,794
It was you.

146
00:10:07,003 --> 00:10:09,630
Not Yi-gyeong or my mom.

147
00:10:09,631 --> 00:10:10,673
It was you.

148
00:10:15,511 --> 00:10:17,763
So, that's how her mom passed away?

149
00:10:17,764 --> 00:10:19,181
The cafe owner on the first floor

150
00:10:19,182 --> 00:10:20,558
was the one who got blamed?

151
00:10:22,101 --> 00:10:23,728
Seon has no clue about any of this?

152
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:25,980
She doesn't know a thing.

153
00:10:26,356 --> 00:10:27,773
And Mr. Kim's building

154
00:10:27,774 --> 00:10:29,566
was bought with Mr. Nam, right?

155
00:10:29,567 --> 00:10:30,360
Yes.

156
00:10:30,652 --> 00:10:32,903
Gosh, that Mr. Nam...

157
00:10:32,904 --> 00:10:35,280
The rumors about him aren't great.

158
00:10:35,281 --> 00:10:37,157
I should have been there with you.

159
00:10:37,158 --> 00:10:39,202
But Yi-gyeong helped a lot.

160
00:10:39,535 --> 00:10:40,453
Yi-gyeong?

161
00:10:43,998 --> 00:10:45,667
So, what about my share?

162
00:10:47,210 --> 00:10:48,210
Your share?

163
00:10:48,211 --> 00:10:49,003
What's that about?

164
00:10:49,963 --> 00:10:51,630
We agreed to split it.

165
00:10:51,631 --> 00:10:54,174
Hey, that's because you called
the cops and messed it up.

166
00:10:54,175 --> 00:10:55,342
I told you, right?

167
00:10:55,343 --> 00:10:57,636
I didn't call the police.
My mother-in-law did.

168
00:10:57,637 --> 00:10:59,514
Oh, this guy is trying to be slick again.

169
00:10:59,806 --> 00:11:01,682
You started it first.

170
00:11:01,683 --> 00:11:03,225
It's the mess you made.

171
00:11:03,226 --> 00:11:06,728
Because of the mess you created,
I had to suffer all alone.

172
00:11:06,729 --> 00:11:08,146
I almost died.

173
00:11:08,147 --> 00:11:09,232
You killed me.

174
00:11:10,024 --> 00:11:13,485
You killed me,
my mother-in-law, and the cafe owner too.

175
00:11:13,486 --> 00:11:15,570
Are you some sort of serial killer?

176
00:11:15,571 --> 00:11:17,114
If you're going to argue like that,

177
00:11:17,115 --> 00:11:20,326
then go and try to become
Dangunwanggum, you bastard!

178
00:11:20,576 --> 00:11:21,703
Seriously.

179
00:11:23,162 --> 00:11:24,372
Hey,

180
00:11:25,790 --> 00:11:27,792
you think I don't know
how much you struggled too?

181
00:11:28,251 --> 00:11:31,337
That's why I came here
right after waking up.

182
00:11:32,171 --> 00:11:34,048
Then, let's do it this way.

183
00:11:34,674 --> 00:11:36,717
Let's talk to our lawyer

184
00:11:36,718 --> 00:11:39,594
and get it notarized
to split the shares, okay?

185
00:11:39,595 --> 00:11:40,555
Does that sound reasonable?

186
00:11:42,765 --> 00:11:44,225
I can't just do whatever I want
with the shares.

187
00:11:44,475 --> 00:11:46,102
They're not personal,
they're corporate.

188
00:11:47,770 --> 00:11:48,603
Corporate?

189
00:11:48,604 --> 00:11:49,272
Yes.

190
00:11:49,439 --> 00:11:50,856
You mean with that Mr. Nam guy?

191
00:11:50,857 --> 00:11:51,482
Yes.

192
00:11:51,941 --> 00:11:54,443
Damn it! Seriously!

193
00:11:54,444 --> 00:11:55,778
You dumb fool!

194
00:11:56,154 --> 00:11:57,779
What are you trusting him for?

195
00:11:57,780 --> 00:11:59,781
Hey, they say
you need a corporation

196
00:11:59,782 --> 00:12:01,825
to be included in the redevelopment,
you fool.

197
00:12:01,826 --> 00:12:03,118
How much are you getting?

198
00:12:03,119 --> 00:12:03,703
Ten billion.

199
00:12:05,496 --> 00:12:06,414
Damn...

200
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:10,375
Hey! We could make
at least 30 billion from that!

201
00:12:10,376 --> 00:12:13,171
I'm really going crazy
because of this dumb fool!

202
00:12:13,421 --> 00:12:17,008
Hey, that's why you get
taken advantage everywhere.

203
00:12:17,842 --> 00:12:19,302
What a frustrating guy.

204
00:12:29,604 --> 00:12:30,313
Yes.

205
00:12:30,772 --> 00:12:32,607
Yes, I'm a pushover.

206
00:12:33,149 --> 00:12:34,609
That's why I get taken advantage of.

207
00:12:35,902 --> 00:12:37,403
My friend takes my wife away too.

208
00:12:39,614 --> 00:12:40,740
What do you mean?

209
00:12:40,907 --> 00:12:41,699
You really don't know?

210
00:12:41,991 --> 00:12:42,700
Huh?

211
00:12:43,618 --> 00:12:44,952
You slept with Seon, right?

212
00:12:47,455 --> 00:12:48,789
Ah...

213
00:12:48,790 --> 00:12:49,665
Hey, hold on.

214
00:12:52,794 --> 00:12:54,629
I just yelled suddenly...

215
00:12:55,254 --> 00:12:56,672
Why is my head hurting like this?

216
00:12:57,382 --> 00:12:59,592
- I should get to the hospital quickly.
- Hold on.

217
00:13:00,134 --> 00:13:01,551
Min Hwal-sung.

218
00:13:01,552 --> 00:13:02,553
Let's have a talk.

219
00:13:03,137 --> 00:13:04,596
Why the rush?

220
00:13:04,597 --> 00:13:06,057
Why did you do that with Seon?

221
00:13:10,478 --> 00:13:11,479
When did you find out?

222
00:13:11,854 --> 00:13:14,565
Are you seriously asking me that?

223
00:13:15,066 --> 00:13:15,775
Hey.

224
00:13:16,401 --> 00:13:17,402
Hey, wait.

225
00:13:18,611 --> 00:13:20,321
Isn't this the golf club
I gave you as a present?

226
00:13:20,947 --> 00:13:21,989
That's right, you bastard!

227
00:13:22,615 --> 00:13:24,574
Okay, okay!

228
00:13:24,575 --> 00:13:26,451
Hey, I'm sorry about Seon!

229
00:13:26,452 --> 00:13:28,036
Should I kneel? I'll get on my knees.

230
00:13:28,037 --> 00:13:29,788
What if Da-rae finds out?

231
00:13:29,789 --> 00:13:30,705
What about Yi-gyeong?

232
00:13:30,706 --> 00:13:31,790
What am I then?

233
00:13:31,791 --> 00:13:34,126
Wait, Su-jong!

234
00:13:34,127 --> 00:13:35,794
Hey, calm down!

235
00:13:35,795 --> 00:13:37,003
How long have you met her, you bastard?

236
00:13:37,004 --> 00:13:38,839
Hey, hey!

237
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:40,632
Hey, if that hits me, I'm dead!

238
00:13:40,633 --> 00:13:42,050
I asked how many times
have you slept with her!

239
00:13:42,051 --> 00:13:43,594
Damn it!

240
00:13:56,649 --> 00:13:57,275
Damn it!

241
00:14:23,968 --> 00:14:25,344
119

242
00:14:41,402 --> 00:14:42,069
Hurry and get him
to the hospital!

243
00:15:09,972 --> 00:15:14,435
SEJEONG-RO TRAFFIC ACCIDENT

244
00:15:19,065 --> 00:15:20,691
Taxi collides with rescue vehicle
on Sejeong-ro, Seoul

245
00:16:17,248 --> 00:16:20,333
- Hey.
- Su-jong, how did you know?

246
00:16:20,334 --> 00:16:23,045
I had a bad dream.

247
00:16:23,713 --> 00:16:24,797
Is he okay?

248
00:16:33,973 --> 00:16:36,600
The MRI results are normal.

249
00:16:36,601 --> 00:16:38,394
His blood levels are normal too.

250
00:16:39,061 --> 00:16:40,771
You could say this is a miracle.

251
00:16:41,272 --> 00:16:44,066
I've never seen this before either.

252
00:16:45,443 --> 00:16:47,277
The patient

253
00:16:47,278 --> 00:16:48,821
sneaked out at night

254
00:16:49,572 --> 00:16:51,949
and seems to have been hit by a car.

255
00:16:52,742 --> 00:16:53,951
Did you say he sneaked out?

256
00:16:54,160 --> 00:16:56,161
I ran a few tests

257
00:16:56,162 --> 00:16:57,913
and there's some memory loss.

258
00:16:58,331 --> 00:17:01,626
Probably because of that,
he went out unknowingly.

259
00:17:01,876 --> 00:17:03,169
Memory loss?

260
00:17:03,669 --> 00:17:06,589
Medically, it's called
transient global amnesia.

261
00:17:07,340 --> 00:17:10,217
In most cases, you recover over time.

262
00:17:10,635 --> 00:17:12,427
If that's in most cases...

263
00:17:12,428 --> 00:17:14,054
Sometimes,

264
00:17:14,055 --> 00:17:16,223
there are instances
where the memory doesn't come back.

265
00:17:17,099 --> 00:17:20,102
Fortunately, the injuries
from the accident are very minor.

266
00:17:27,026 --> 00:17:28,027
Yi-gyeong!

267
00:17:28,132 --> 00:17:29,444
Please sit down.

268
00:17:29,445 --> 00:17:30,404
Hey, just sit down.

269
00:17:32,073 --> 00:17:32,907
My gosh.

270
00:17:35,201 --> 00:17:36,409
Wait a second.

271
00:17:36,410 --> 00:17:37,870
Huh? What is it?

272
00:17:39,372 --> 00:17:40,915
Don't you remember?

273
00:17:43,501 --> 00:17:44,960
I really don't know.

274
00:17:45,711 --> 00:17:46,879
What time is it now?

275
00:17:47,421 --> 00:17:51,175
I mean, I know there was
a party for your mom's birthday, right?

276
00:17:53,844 --> 00:17:55,179
I was kidnapped.

277
00:17:55,763 --> 00:17:56,764
Don't you remember?

278
00:17:58,933 --> 00:17:59,892
Kidnapped?

279
00:18:00,267 --> 00:18:01,644
What happened?

280
00:18:02,895 --> 00:18:04,145
Yi-gyeong, are you okay?

281
00:18:04,146 --> 00:18:05,606
So, did they catch the culprit?

282
00:18:08,150 --> 00:18:09,026
Hwal-sung.

283
00:18:10,611 --> 00:18:12,570
Do you

284
00:18:12,571 --> 00:18:13,364
remember me?

285
00:18:15,366 --> 00:18:16,575
Aren't you Gi Su-jong?

286
00:18:18,994 --> 00:18:20,329
Hey, come on.

287
00:18:20,621 --> 00:18:21,955
Man.

288
00:18:21,956 --> 00:18:23,290
Why would I not know you?

289
00:18:23,541 --> 00:18:26,001
Hey, it's nice to see you.

290
00:18:26,752 --> 00:18:28,169
Your mom.

291
00:18:28,170 --> 00:18:30,423
You should call your mom right away.
We need to greet her.

292
00:18:31,507 --> 00:18:32,341
What?

293
00:18:34,844 --> 00:18:35,678
What's wrong?

294
00:18:36,971 --> 00:18:38,139
Did something happen?

295
00:18:39,515 --> 00:18:40,474
She passed away.

296
00:18:43,811 --> 00:18:46,105
Huh? What do you mean?

297
00:18:47,064 --> 00:18:49,066
I'll tell you later.

298
00:18:49,859 --> 00:18:51,110
What do you mean later?

299
00:18:53,863 --> 00:18:54,863
Your mom...

300
00:18:54,864 --> 00:18:56,282
Why did your mom pass away?

301
00:18:58,117 --> 00:18:59,577
That doesn't make sense.

302
00:19:02,872 --> 00:19:03,956
Jeez...

303
00:19:07,752 --> 00:19:08,878
Why...

304
00:19:09,462 --> 00:19:10,463
Yi-gyeong...

305
00:19:13,174 --> 00:19:16,051
Mother...

306
00:19:18,596 --> 00:19:20,389
Mother...

307
00:19:23,100 --> 00:19:25,895
Mother...

308
00:19:29,023 --> 00:19:31,025
Mother...

309
00:19:34,028 --> 00:19:34,987
Doctor.

310
00:19:36,363 --> 00:19:37,907
When can I get discharged?

311
00:19:38,324 --> 00:19:40,241
I'm worried about leaving

312
00:19:40,242 --> 00:19:42,035
my wife home alone, you know?

313
00:19:42,036 --> 00:19:43,120
I'm really worried.

314
00:19:43,746 --> 00:19:45,206
I think I need to leave soon.

315
00:19:45,790 --> 00:19:46,582
Please?

316
00:19:49,251 --> 00:19:51,420
Yi-gyeong, I'm sorry.

317
00:19:52,755 --> 00:19:54,215
Hwal-sung is awake?

318
00:19:54,507 --> 00:19:55,925
They say it's a miracle.

319
00:19:57,635 --> 00:19:59,677
Wait, didn't you say
he was in a coma?

320
00:19:59,678 --> 00:20:01,013
But he woke up suddenly?

321
00:20:01,388 --> 00:20:03,473
That's why they said
it was like a miracle.

322
00:20:03,474 --> 00:20:04,642
But he has no memory.

323
00:20:05,518 --> 00:20:06,769
No memory?

324
00:20:07,728 --> 00:20:10,730
I think they said
it was global transient amnesia.

325
00:20:10,731 --> 00:20:12,440
Transient global amnesia.

326
00:20:12,441 --> 00:20:13,274
Oh.

327
00:20:13,275 --> 00:20:14,192
Right.

328
00:20:14,193 --> 00:20:15,652
But is that an actual condition?

329
00:20:15,653 --> 00:20:16,403
Yes.

330
00:20:16,529 --> 00:20:18,531
Hmm...

331
00:20:19,698 --> 00:20:20,783
Oh, Da-rae.

332
00:20:29,208 --> 00:20:31,418
Uncle Hwal-sung is awake.

333
00:20:31,752 --> 00:20:32,920
He's doing well.

334
00:20:33,629 --> 00:20:36,257
Really? That's fantastic!

335
00:20:36,841 --> 00:20:37,925
Yes.

336
00:20:44,390 --> 00:20:49,103
But what's
wrong with both of your expressions?

337
00:20:51,438 --> 00:20:53,399
- Why? How do we look?
- Huh?

338
00:20:54,358 --> 00:20:55,276
Huh?

339
00:20:55,776 --> 00:20:57,278
Us two? Why?

340
00:20:57,570 --> 00:21:01,907
It looks like
you both saw something awful.

341
00:21:02,408 --> 00:21:04,577
- No.
- No, not at all.

342
00:21:04,910 --> 00:21:05,703
Eat up.

343
00:21:08,747 --> 00:21:11,375
Can we talk for a second?

344
00:21:12,418 --> 00:21:13,252
Yes.

345
00:21:13,836 --> 00:21:15,045
- You should eat too.
- Okay.

346
00:21:18,048 --> 00:21:19,174
Mother.

347
00:21:25,264 --> 00:21:26,807
Hwal-sung is here.

348
00:21:28,183 --> 00:21:29,351
Your clumsy son-in-law.

349
00:21:30,144 --> 00:21:31,228
I'm late...

350
00:21:34,023 --> 00:21:35,566
I'm late in greeting you.

351
00:21:38,110 --> 00:21:39,528
Your unfulfilled dreams...

352
00:21:41,780 --> 00:21:43,449
I'll make them come true.

353
00:21:54,418 --> 00:21:56,836
Hmm...

354
00:21:56,837 --> 00:21:59,924
So, what happened
to the Pyeong-buk Gwan?

355
00:22:00,883 --> 00:22:02,383
Did you sell it while I was gone?

356
00:22:02,384 --> 00:22:03,802
Why do you care?

357
00:22:04,595 --> 00:22:07,805
Oh, now that your mom's gone,

358
00:22:07,806 --> 00:22:09,515
we need to manage the assets well.

359
00:22:09,516 --> 00:22:10,517
Min Hwal-sung.

360
00:22:11,101 --> 00:22:12,102
Don't be so cocky.

361
00:22:15,314 --> 00:22:17,608
Yi-gyeong, what's wrong?

362
00:22:18,609 --> 00:22:20,903
I just mean we should
work together as a couple.

363
00:22:24,740 --> 00:22:26,241
Now that your mother has passed,

364
00:22:26,992 --> 00:22:28,243
I know you're upset.

365
00:22:29,703 --> 00:22:31,329
But even so,

366
00:22:31,330 --> 00:22:34,375
if a couple puts their heads together,
there's nothing we can't handle, right?

367
00:22:35,751 --> 00:22:37,878
What can we even
discuss with a vegetable?

368
00:22:41,256 --> 00:22:42,174
That's true.

369
00:22:46,095 --> 00:22:48,472
But I'm still here by your side.

370
00:22:51,976 --> 00:22:53,435
Aren't you glad I'm awake?

371
00:23:00,442 --> 00:23:02,068
Have these while we talk.

372
00:23:02,069 --> 00:23:03,070
Thank you.

373
00:23:07,992 --> 00:23:09,534
You saw the will
last time, right?

374
00:23:09,535 --> 00:23:12,121
I need your signature
for the asset inheritance.

375
00:23:13,038 --> 00:23:15,206
Do I need to read all of this?

376
00:23:15,207 --> 00:23:17,084
No, that's not necessary.

377
00:23:18,002 --> 00:23:19,670
The assets are pretty varied,

378
00:23:20,087 --> 00:23:22,756
so there are tax issues
and some things to handle.

379
00:23:23,507 --> 00:23:25,508
You also had that property

380
00:23:25,509 --> 00:23:26,468
related to redevelopment.

381
00:23:27,428 --> 00:23:28,679
That's right.

382
00:23:36,687 --> 00:23:38,814
Please handle
everything well, sir.

383
00:23:41,150 --> 00:23:41,942
Sure.

384
00:23:43,819 --> 00:23:45,403
Just make sure

385
00:23:45,404 --> 00:23:46,321
to take care of it properly.

386
00:23:46,947 --> 00:23:49,033
I'll get back to you once it's sorted.

387
00:23:57,875 --> 00:23:59,417
But don't you think
this is a bit rash?

388
00:23:59,418 --> 00:24:01,919
You should read it carefully
before signing.

389
00:24:01,920 --> 00:24:03,087
You never know.

390
00:24:03,088 --> 00:24:04,839
What do you mean
you never know?

391
00:24:04,840 --> 00:24:07,259
They have been with Mom for a long time.

392
00:24:07,926 --> 00:24:09,970
I got this, so don't worry.

393
00:24:12,139 --> 00:24:13,390
Well, I guess

394
00:24:14,224 --> 00:24:15,809
you know what's best.

395
00:24:22,566 --> 00:24:23,567
Not hungry?

396
00:24:27,905 --> 00:24:29,198
Let me wash my hands.

397
00:24:40,876 --> 00:24:43,169
Good job, Attorney Yang.

398
00:24:43,170 --> 00:24:44,046
See you soon.

399
00:24:49,301 --> 00:24:50,302
Gosh.

400
00:24:51,678 --> 00:24:52,971
Did you check my DM?

401
00:24:54,306 --> 00:24:55,390
Let's meet up.

402
00:25:07,611 --> 00:25:09,571
Is it possible
to watch over one person?

403
00:25:10,906 --> 00:25:11,657
Who?

404
00:25:12,116 --> 00:25:13,158
My husband.

405
00:25:15,702 --> 00:25:17,412
This seems to be the right place.

406
00:25:18,872 --> 00:25:19,873
Where are you?

407
00:25:20,499 --> 00:25:21,500
The third one.

408
00:25:21,875 --> 00:25:22,835
The third?

409
00:25:30,008 --> 00:25:31,385
Why so shocked? You're not an old man.

410
00:25:32,010 --> 00:25:32,970
Sit down.

411
00:25:34,012 --> 00:25:35,138
These are yours.

412
00:25:35,139 --> 00:25:36,807
- I'm fine, thanks.
- What do you mean?

413
00:25:37,474 --> 00:25:38,684
I'm wearing mine.

414
00:25:41,270 --> 00:25:43,230
By the way...

415
00:25:44,356 --> 00:25:47,191
Ever since my mother-in-law passed away,
you're looking much better.

416
00:25:47,192 --> 00:25:48,943
Oh, yes.

417
00:25:48,944 --> 00:25:50,487
The embezzlement
hasn't been discovered yet?

418
00:25:51,280 --> 00:25:54,074
Why are we suddenly talking about this?

419
00:25:54,825 --> 00:25:57,619
Did you fix the inheritance documents
like I mentioned?

420
00:25:59,037 --> 00:26:02,498
Yes.
It'll be under your name soon.

421
00:26:02,499 --> 00:26:04,168
Okay, good job.

422
00:26:05,627 --> 00:26:08,172
But is this really okay?

423
00:26:09,631 --> 00:26:10,924
Of course, it's okay.

424
00:26:12,342 --> 00:26:14,428
Just trust me.
I have everything planned.

425
00:26:15,637 --> 00:26:16,679
Come here.

426
00:26:16,680 --> 00:26:17,931
Let's take a commemorative photo.

427
00:26:18,223 --> 00:26:19,308
Try this on.

428
00:26:20,559 --> 00:26:21,643
- It looks good.
- What are you doing?

429
00:26:45,500 --> 00:26:46,960
Wow, look at this.

430
00:26:47,502 --> 00:26:49,046
This circuit breaker
keeps tripping, right?

431
00:26:50,255 --> 00:26:53,050
That's because of a leak.

432
00:26:54,343 --> 00:26:56,469
How much will it be to fix this?

433
00:26:56,470 --> 00:26:57,762
Hmm...

434
00:26:57,763 --> 00:26:59,639
It's serious.

435
00:26:59,640 --> 00:27:02,976
We need to fix the water tank
and the panel.

436
00:27:03,810 --> 00:27:05,604
So how much is it going to cost?

437
00:27:06,104 --> 00:27:08,147
Well,
it's pretty old as well.

438
00:27:08,148 --> 00:27:10,150
Why are you
setting me up like this?

439
00:27:11,778 --> 00:27:13,694
It's going to cost around 10 million.

440
00:27:13,695 --> 00:27:15,446
- 10 million won?
- Yes.

441
00:27:15,447 --> 00:27:17,658
That's actually considered cheap.

442
00:27:18,367 --> 00:27:19,742
In that case,

443
00:27:19,743 --> 00:27:21,578
at least fix it
so that the lights are working.

444
00:27:22,371 --> 00:27:25,373
Well, I can do
some emergency fixes,

445
00:27:25,374 --> 00:27:27,541
but later on, it will be really dangerous.

446
00:27:27,542 --> 00:27:29,086
Everything needs to be replaced.

447
00:27:29,461 --> 00:27:31,504
I got it. We can do that later.

448
00:27:31,505 --> 00:27:34,382
For now, just do some emergency repairs.

449
00:27:34,383 --> 00:27:36,843
It's way too old.

450
00:27:39,054 --> 00:27:41,305
You need to replace
all of this, okay?

451
00:27:41,306 --> 00:27:41,806
Okay.

452
00:27:41,807 --> 00:27:44,393
- I'll get going.
- Yes, take care.

453
00:27:46,186 --> 00:27:49,439
Gosh, I don't have 10 million won.

454
00:28:05,872 --> 00:28:06,623
What's going on?

455
00:28:06,999 --> 00:28:09,376
Oh, you seem busy.

456
00:28:10,085 --> 00:28:11,128
What are you doing here?

457
00:28:12,462 --> 00:28:13,671
It smells bad.

458
00:28:13,672 --> 00:28:14,464
What?

459
00:28:14,840 --> 00:28:17,301
Maybe it's because we're underground?

460
00:28:36,653 --> 00:28:37,821
Where are we going now?

461
00:28:38,613 --> 00:28:39,698
Do you have any last words?

462
00:28:40,741 --> 00:28:41,491
What?

463
00:28:41,992 --> 00:28:45,245
The last words
you want to say to your family.

464
00:28:52,252 --> 00:28:53,754
I'm just joking.

465
00:28:58,258 --> 00:29:00,802
Mr. Nam said he wants to see you.

466
00:29:02,220 --> 00:29:03,764
Do you work with Mr. Nam?

467
00:29:04,097 --> 00:29:05,057
Since when?

468
00:29:05,974 --> 00:29:06,975
Jonah.

469
00:29:08,810 --> 00:29:10,854
Do you know what my name means?

470
00:29:11,938 --> 00:29:12,939
Jonah.

471
00:29:14,900 --> 00:29:16,610
A person who brings misfortune.

472
00:29:19,112 --> 00:29:20,072
So?

473
00:29:20,614 --> 00:29:21,656
You remember, right?

474
00:29:22,407 --> 00:29:26,078
The pain that can't kill you
makes you stronger.

475
00:29:28,163 --> 00:29:29,331
What does that mean?

476
00:29:30,874 --> 00:29:33,377
Contact me anytime if you need help.

477
00:29:45,639 --> 00:29:47,264
You're friends
with this guy, right?

478
00:29:47,265 --> 00:29:49,351
Yes, we're best friends.
We're tight.

479
00:29:50,185 --> 00:29:51,103
What are you going to do?

480
00:29:52,562 --> 00:29:54,397
What if he holds out?

481
00:29:54,398 --> 00:29:56,148
But he's the type who talks first anyway.

482
00:29:56,149 --> 00:29:57,400
You don't need to worry too much.

483
00:29:57,401 --> 00:29:58,651
Hmm...

484
00:29:58,652 --> 00:30:01,946
Why hasn't that daughter been in touch?

485
00:30:01,947 --> 00:30:03,989
Even with extra cash, not even a reply.

486
00:30:03,990 --> 00:30:05,575
Is it because she's Generation MZ?

487
00:30:05,909 --> 00:30:08,286
You need to handle Pyeong-buk Gwan well.

488
00:30:08,703 --> 00:30:10,288
You have to protect its pride.

489
00:30:11,748 --> 00:30:12,749
Pyeong-buk Gwan?

490
00:30:13,500 --> 00:30:14,584
Proceed with it.

491
00:30:15,502 --> 00:30:16,710
Wow.

492
00:30:16,711 --> 00:30:18,880
I have the money,
so just persuade them.

493
00:30:19,631 --> 00:30:22,467
We'll definitely protect its pride, okay?

494
00:30:27,013 --> 00:30:28,390
Then, how about some shares...

495
00:30:29,516 --> 00:30:30,266
Shares?

496
00:30:30,267 --> 00:30:31,101
Yes.

497
00:30:31,768 --> 00:30:34,437
If I can persuade Pyeong-buk Gwan,

498
00:30:34,438 --> 00:30:35,814
I'll take half the shares.

499
00:30:36,690 --> 00:30:39,568
The same thing with Han-maum too.
After Pyeong-buk Gwan is acquired,

500
00:30:40,152 --> 00:30:42,779
most of the changed land
is mine to secure.

501
00:30:43,155 --> 00:30:44,948
So of course, I should get more shares.

502
00:30:46,032 --> 00:30:47,700
Oh,

503
00:30:47,701 --> 00:30:50,119
you're quite the competitor, Mr. Gi.

504
00:30:50,120 --> 00:30:51,204
Not at all, really.

505
00:30:55,375 --> 00:30:56,251
Okay.

506
00:30:57,586 --> 00:30:58,587
Let's think about it.

507
00:30:58,753 --> 00:31:01,590
Yes, please consider it. I'll get going.

508
00:31:01,965 --> 00:31:03,300
Oh, by the way,

509
00:31:03,800 --> 00:31:04,676
what are you doing tomorrow?

510
00:31:06,511 --> 00:31:07,971
Why do you ask about tomorrow?

511
00:31:20,609 --> 00:31:21,985
What is this?
Are you getting married?

512
00:31:22,986 --> 00:31:25,070
REDEVELOPMENT PROJECT / PRIVATE DINNER

513
00:31:25,071 --> 00:31:27,824
It's a gathering for couples,
so dress nicely.

514
00:31:28,950 --> 00:31:29,743
Take care.

515
00:31:30,243 --> 00:31:31,619
Oh, sure.

516
00:31:31,620 --> 00:31:32,370
Yes.

517
00:31:43,548 --> 00:31:44,925
Did you hear that punk talking?

518
00:31:45,550 --> 00:31:46,717
Anyway,

519
00:31:46,718 --> 00:31:48,887
the black beast
isn't just something you gather up.

520
00:31:49,429 --> 00:31:50,971
After the work is done,

521
00:31:50,972 --> 00:31:52,224
take care of him too.

522
00:31:59,105 --> 00:31:59,981
Didn't you hear me?

523
00:32:03,026 --> 00:32:05,237
I did hear. I'll take care of it.

524
00:32:09,449 --> 00:32:10,533
Honey.

525
00:32:10,534 --> 00:32:12,118
Do I really have to go too?

526
00:32:12,410 --> 00:32:14,079
Yes, you have to go.

527
00:32:16,122 --> 00:32:18,917
How is there
only workout clothes in here?

528
00:32:20,126 --> 00:32:22,170
Seon, where's my suit jacket?

529
00:32:23,004 --> 00:32:25,465
It's in that inner box,
underneath the blanket

530
00:32:34,724 --> 00:32:36,768
Is this too much? How does it look?

531
00:32:38,228 --> 00:32:39,396
Wow.

532
00:32:39,980 --> 00:32:41,690
Kim Seon, you look beautiful.

533
00:32:42,899 --> 00:32:43,733
What are you saying?

534
00:32:44,067 --> 00:32:44,985
Is it really okay?

535
00:32:47,571 --> 00:32:49,280
Jeez.

536
00:32:49,281 --> 00:32:51,241
Since you're pretty,
you got with Hwal-sung.

537
00:32:53,201 --> 00:32:55,245
Why suddenly bring that up?

538
00:32:55,787 --> 00:32:57,956
It just suddenly came in my head.

539
00:32:59,291 --> 00:33:01,126
Why with you and Hwal-sung...

540
00:33:03,003 --> 00:33:04,087
Jeez.

541
00:33:05,505 --> 00:33:06,381
Honey.

542
00:33:07,674 --> 00:33:10,594
Just forget about it.
Erase it from your memory.

543
00:33:11,469 --> 00:33:12,345
Got it?

544
00:33:14,681 --> 00:33:16,349
- Okay?
- Yes, okay.

545
00:33:21,980 --> 00:33:25,441
Let's hurry up and go, okay?

546
00:33:25,442 --> 00:33:26,651
- This one?
- Yes.

547
00:33:40,749 --> 00:33:41,249
LOAN HEAVEN

548
00:33:50,675 --> 00:33:51,509
The IV is almost done.

549
00:33:53,345 --> 00:33:54,179
Yi-gyeong,

550
00:33:55,305 --> 00:33:56,973
I heard from Seon.

551
00:33:57,474 --> 00:33:58,849
How many weeks did you say?

552
00:33:58,850 --> 00:34:00,268
It's been a little over two months.

